    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0217",
      "sequence": 229,
      "meaning": "Janaka said, ‘Sage, seeing your feet today, I cannot express the power of my merit. These beautiful dark and fair brothers give joy even to joy. Their pure, mutually delightful love cannot be described. Hear me, lord,’ Videha continued gladly, ‘their natural affection is like that of Brahman and the individual self.’ The king gazed at the Lord again and again, his body thrilled and his heart increasingly elated. Praising the sage and bowing at his feet, the lord of the earth escorted him into the city. The king gave them lodging in a handsome residence comfortable in every season, completed worship and every form of service, then took leave and returned home. After dining and resting with the seers, the jewel of Raghu’s line sat with his brother; about one watch of daylight remained.",
