    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0218",
      "sequence": 230,
      "meaning": "A strong longing arose in Lakṣmaṇa’s heart to go and see Janakpur, but out of reverence for the Lord and reserve before the sage he did not say it aloud and only smiled inwardly. Rāma understood his younger brother’s mind, and love for his devotee surged in his heart. Humbly smiling, he spoke after receiving the teacher’s discipline: ‘Lord, Lakṣmaṇa wishes to see the city but, from deference and fear, does not say so. If I receive your permission, I shall show him the city and bring him back at once.’ Hearing this, the sage affectionately replied, ‘Why would you not preserve good conduct, Rāma? You are the guardian bridge of righteousness, dear child, and, overcome by love, the giver of joy to servants. Go, you two repositories of delight, see the city and let everyone’s eyes bear fruit by showing them your beautiful faces.’",
