    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0219",
      "sequence": 231,
      "meaning": "Bowing at the sage’s lotus feet, the two brothers set out, giving joy to every eye. Groups of boys, captivated in eye and mind by their great beauty, joined them. Yellow garments wrapped their waists, quivers were fastened there, and graceful bows and arrows shone in their hands. Fine streaks of sandal paste suited their bodies; dark and fair, they made an enchanting pair. With lion-like necks, broad arms, splendid jewel necklaces on their chests, beautiful golden lotus-eyes and moonlike faces that removed the three afflictions, they stole the mind of everyone they glanced at. Golden flower earrings lent beauty to their ears; their graceful sidelong gaze, arched brows and tilaka line shone brilliantly. Fine cloth adorned their heads over dark curling hair: from nails to crown the two brothers embodied all beauty in a lovely land.",
