    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0220",
      "sequence": 232,
      "meaning": "The townspeople learned that the princes had come to see the city. Abandoning every household task, they ran as though paupers were looting a treasure. Gazing on the naturally beautiful brothers, they were happy to receive the fruit of having eyes. Young women crowded the palace windows, lovingly contemplating Rāma’s form and telling one another, ‘Friend, these two have conquered the beauty of millions of Loves. Among gods, humans, demons, nāgas and sages, beauty like this has never been heard of. Viṣṇu has four arms, Brahmā four faces, and Śiva five faces and a formidable guise. There is no other god with whom, friend, we can compare this beauty. These dark and fair adolescents are homes of loveliness and abodes of joy; upon every limb one could offer up hundreds of millions of Loves.’",
